  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Adds generated FmpzMatrix row and column selectors through the existing resource-plus-packed-slice declaration system. Both selectors preserve order and duplicates, validate checked result dimensions and every index before owned-result initialization, retain all zero-dimensional orientations, deep-copy exact entries, report retained native memory, and close deterministically. Dynamic differential tests cover large exact entries, duplicate and out-of-order indices, closed owners, zero shapes, buffer-length mismatch, invalid-index failure atomicity, and successful recovery after failures. The lifecycle harness passes 300 generated-adapter rounds plus 1,000 C rounds under ASan, UBSan, and leak detection. On the development host, selecting 250 rows or columns from a 500 by 500 small-entry matrix takes about 0.39--0.40 ms, versus 12.2--13.4 ms for the former incremental generated-resource route, a 31--34 times speedup.",
    "risks": [
      "FmpzMatrix resources and these selectors remain wasm=False; the public portable matrix implementation must retain its tested capability fallback until opaque-resource WebAssembly lowering exists.",
      "This shared declaration lane deliberately does not edit public matrix.py, so public dense ZZ row and column selection continues using the incremental resource route until the integration follow-up switches it to the generated bulk calls.",
      "The sub-millisecond measurements are development-host evidence rather than a cross-machine hard limit; the benchmark also reports the same-process former route so relative regressions remain visible.",
      "ASan and UBSan lifecycle execution is a Unix capability; Windows runs the ordinary generated-adapter ownership and failure tests but reports sanitizers unavailable."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Route public Matrix.matrix_from_rows and matrix_from_columns for generated dense ZZ resources through these declarations using a single UInt64Buffer crossing.",
      "Add the public 500 by 500 selection workload to the dense integer performance ratchet after routing and remove the documented incremental-selector cliff.",
      "Enable the unchanged declaration for WebAssembly when generated opaque-resource lowering and lifecycle tests are available."
    ]
  }
}
